#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186283864 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0cbb889-0fe1-5347-94a3-53db3ff9a95c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Vertices of a Polygon Given Its Image Under a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98744a46-1ddc-5d16-939d-fc52da67c11f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283866} {:answer/id #uuid "0f0cf815-df8d-5406-801e-49e27bdf5726" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283867} {:answer/id #uuid "a816077d-0b79-5326-b761-d4032a5bdc86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283868} {:answer/id #uuid "f3e6c023-fced-5e51-9290-8d99c38b7209" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283869} {:answer/id #uuid "27b17022-e430-5321-a4f4-dcc39497578a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283870}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98744a46-1ddc-5d16-939d-fc52da67c11f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283866} :answer-field/id #uuid "da278268-0953-57c8-8371-23abd5230202" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283865}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cf0d1bd1-6767-5355-bf10-b6a1baf057d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-85172" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 10 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe triangle $S$ is mapped to the triangle ${S}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The triangle ${S}^{′}$ has vertices $(10,5),(0,-5),$ and $(15,20).$ Which of the following are vertices of $S?$\n\n- $(9,5)$\n- $(0,1)$\n- $(10,-7)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${S}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=[\\begin{aligned}10 & 0 & 15 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 20\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $S$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =[\\begin{aligned}10 & 0 & 15 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 20\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}10 & 0 & 15 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 20\\end{aligned}] \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}10 & 0 & 15 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 20\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{35-30}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -10 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -10 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}10 & 0 & 15 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 20\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -10 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}10 & 0 & 15 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 20\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 50 & -125 \\\\ 5 & -35 & 95\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 10 & -25 \\\\ 1 & -7 & 19\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of the vertices of the original triangle are $(0,1),(10,-7),(-25,19).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}]}
